oker for a more critical moment (like when I need to regain control or when the Landlord is down to few cards) would be more strategic.\n\nReason:\nI choose to **pass**. While I could play BlackJoker to beat the ♣2, this would be a poor use of one of the game\'s strongest cards. The BlackJoker should be reserved for critical situations where I need to guarantee control, especially later in the game when card counts are lower. By passing now, I preserve this powerful card for when it can have maximum impact, such as helping my teammate finish their hand or preventing the Landlord from going out. The game is still early enough (all players have 11-12 cards) that giving up this one trick is acceptable.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
